Everywhere, where non-null is expected for the expression "originTimeout == null ? requestTimeout : originTimeout" (e.g., at dereference sites), cast the expression to non-null, to prevent follow-on NullAway errors. 
However, if you would have to add many casts, prefer casting at definition time or reassigning the expression to a local variable and casting there, if this is possible without breaking the code.

